## At a glance

| Dimension | Latitude | Tracify |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Framework integration** | Deep | Generic |
| **Evaluation** | Limited, manual | Integrated, automated |
| **Cost tracking** | Basic | Real-time per-call |
| **Best for** | Framework developers | Production iteration |
| **Production readiness** | Good for tracing | Complete all-in-one |

Latitude is best for understanding framework execution during development. Tracify is best for production quality gates and cost optimization.

## Core choice: visibility vs. validation

**Latitude** shows *what your agent did* at the framework level. **Tracify** validates *what your agent achieved* at the outcome level.

## Scenario 1: development with 10+ tools

You need to understand tool selection and decision paths.

**With Latitude:** Detailed framework traces, decision trees, state transitions. Excellent for debugging.

**With Tracify:** Test cases and automatic regression detection. Catches failures automatically.

## Scenario 2: production with cost and quality constraints

Your agent handles 50k requests/month, cost < $0.30, quality > 95%.

**With Latitude:** Manual quality gates and cost breakdown. Expensive and slow.

**With Tracify:** Automated quality gates, real-time cost per-call, regression detection built-in.

## Cost comparison: 50k/month

**Latitude:** $7,900/month ($94,800/year) including manual quality review
**Tracify:** $1,600/month ($19,200/year) all-in-one

Tracify is 5x cheaper because evaluation is included.

## When to choose each

Choose **Latitude** for: framework debugging during development
Choose **Tracify** for: production quality gates and cost optimization

## Action checklist

- [ ] Determine: framework understanding or production quality?
- [ ] If development: evaluate Latitude for 2-3 weeks
- [ ] If production: build Tracify test suite (2-3 days)
- [ ] Calculate true cost including manual work
- [ ] Run both platforms in parallel
- [ ] Measure evaluation velocity and savings
- [ ] Make your choice

## FAQ

{% faq-item question="Does Latitude track costs?" answer="Latitude captures tokens but requires external integration for cost calculations." /%}

{% faq-item question="Can I use both?" answer="Yes, send traces to both platforms. Low overhead, benefits of both." /%}

{% faq-item question="Is Latitude worth the complexity?" answer="Yes for development, but production quality gates favor Tracify." /%}

{% faq-item question="What's Latitude's main limitation?" answer="No integrated evaluation or cost tracking for production." /%}

{% faq-item question="Should I stay with Latitude?" answer="If you need framework depth, yes. If you need production quality gates, Tracify is worth considering." /%}
